A root component's own state, on every target.

`component main root { … }` renders windows rather than widgets, and
`main()` at the root of the file is what renders it. A root component is an
ordinary declaration: nothing lifts its windows, so `passNoInlineComponents`
substitutes the whole body into the package body and renames what it declares
per instantiation, exactly as it does for every other component. `hits__inst0`
is that rename, and what each target emits for it below is the shape it emits
for the package's own state -- a Model field on bubbletea and fyne, a
`remember { mutableStateOf }` on android, an entry in html's `state` object.

The instantiation is load-bearing: a root component nobody renders renders
nothing and declares nothing. It used to be lifted instead -- passRootWindow
scanned every declaration for the root family and emptied it whether or not
anything rendered it, leaving the vars and funcs behind on a shell no backend
reads. `var hits = 0` reached none of them: html emitted `var state = {}`, and
the read of it rendered against a binding the page never declared (#215).

A *timer* in that body is not covered here and is no longer dropped: nothing
clears a body now, so one written there or at the root of a file reaches the
backend that schedules it. testdata/timer_at_package_root.txtar is that.

`bump` reaches no target at all, and that is the right answer: it is pure,
`passInlinePure` folds its one call, and the shake then has a declaration
nothing names. It used to be emitted because `ir.Window.Funcs` was a shake
root, so the hoist kept alive a func the program had already finished with.
root_component_mutating_func.txtar is the archive where a root component's
func survives to every backend, and where the receiver it is *not* spelled
with is asserted.

deny * `(?i)\bbump\b` -- a pure func whose only call was folded reaches no backend; the hoist used to keep it alive as a shake root
deny out/none/html/index.html `var state = \{\s*\}` -- the state is the window's now; an empty state object is the bug this fixture is for

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

component main root {
    var hits = 0

    func bump(n int) => n + 1

    ui.window #page(title="t") {
        ui.text(value="{hits}")
        ui.button(text="go", @click { hits = bump(hits) })
    }
}

main()
